# union.mdc

These rules apply to anything meant for Local 10 union dashboards or union tools.
Read and follow every time you touch dashboard work.

## Non-negotiables

- Mobile-first. Works great on a phone.
- Glove-friendly / dirty-hand friendly:
  - Huge buttons.
  - Big text.
  - Lots of spacing.
  - Nothing tiny.
- High contrast. Easy to read in bad lighting.
- Clean layout. No clutter.
- Works offline whenever possible.
- Prefer **one single HTML file** per dashboard page.

## Charles is always #1

At the very top of every dashboard page, put the biggest, most obvious red call button:

- Label: **CALL CHARLES GRINSTEAD**
- Show number: **(612-428-8004)**
- Link: `tel:6124288004`

Also include a one-tap text button nearby:

- Label: **TEXT CHARLES**
- Link: `sms:6124288004`

Charles must be the most prominent item on the page. Always.

## Tabs and navigation

- Use simple tabs for sections (example: Contacts / Updates / Resources).
- Tabs must be big and easy to hit.
- Keep the number of tabs small (3-5).

## One-tap actions everywhere

- Phone numbers: use `tel:` links.
- Text: use `sms:` links.
- If there's an address: include a one-tap map link (Google/Apple compatible).

## File/folder shape

- Union dashboard lives at root: `index.html`
